            "value": "<div data-page-id=\"WC9GdWptxodM3rxqUu4lYwk6gDd\" data-lark-html-role=\"root\" data-docx-has-block-data=\"false\">\n<div class=\"ace-line ace-line old-record-id-P5wYdIQbdoSLCzxWocilpJDXgJX\">As for the remaining categories, arts and business programmes in Country A were priced at $12,000 and $14,000, in that order. These figures rose to $17,200 and $15,698 in Country B, while Country C recorded the highest tuition for both subjects at an identical rate of $21,783. In terms of accommodation with meals, Country A offered the lowest cost at $8,000, which was approximately $3,000 less than Country B's figure of $11,256. Country C, on the other hand, required students to pay the most for living expenses, at $17,345, more than double that of Country A.</div>\n</div>",
